# Keep the build context small and secret-free. Mirrors .gitignore, plus things an image never needs.
.git
.github
.changeset
.claude
.turbo
.vscode
.idea

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log

# Secrets must never reach a build context, layer or image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/.aws
**/secrets
**/*.tfstate*
**/*.tfvars

.data
tmp
# The model files of the compose bundle: gigabytes an image never carries (ADR-0065).
deploy/models
docs
**/*.md
# What the image carries of the repository itself: its overview and its notices (deploy/Dockerfile).
!README.md
!LICENSE.md
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!TRADEMARKS.md
# The documentation the web UI renders into its pages at build time: docs/nav.json and every file
# it names, wherever it lives. A test of the web app (apps/web/dev/docs.test.ts) keeps this in step.
!docs/nav.json
!docs/guide/*.md
!docs/specs/*.md
!deploy/README.md
!packages/cli/README.md
# What says which commit the image is built from, for the version its server says (ADR-0134): the
# head of the checkout and the branches it may name. Nothing else of .git: not its settings, which
# may hold a credential, and not its history. Kept last, so that no rule above takes a branch away
# for its name.
!.git/HEAD
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs/heads/**
